I go near the entrance.
There is a big wooden counter there.
An elderly gentleman is sitting behind the counter.
He is the cashier.
I stand close to the counter.
I smile and greet him.
"Namaskar Kaka," I say respectfully.
"Namaskar Madam," he says with a smile.
Then I look down at the counter.
There is a big glass on the counter.
There is a menu under that glass.
It is a handwritten menu.
I read that menu carefully.
There are many old dishes on the menu.
I am very hungry.
I want something to eat.
Will I get good tea here?
I think about my order.
